          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "título from Latin titulus, \"an inscription, a label\" (EtymDB 2.1) — a learned borrowing: the stress stays on the first syllable and the -t- between vowels is kept. Worn down through Catalan or Occitan, the same Latin word gave tilde, the name of the accent mark."
            }
          ]
        },
